{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.meta_title'|trans }}{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.meta_description'|trans }}{% endblock %}
{% block og_title %}{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.meta_title'|trans }}{% endblock %}
{% block og_description %}{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.meta_description'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    {% include '_partials/breadcrumb.html.twig' with {
        trail: [
            { label: 'layout.breadcrumb.home'|trans, route: 'app_home' },
            { label: 'guides.index.title'|trans, route: 'app_guides_index' },
            { label: 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.title'|trans, route: null },
        ]
    } %}

    {% include 'guides/_hero_header.html.twig' with { icon: 'navigation', i18n_prefix: 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand' } %}

    <div id="guide-google-maps-to-osmand" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-route">{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.convert_cta'|trans }}</p>
        <div
            id="convert-hero-root"
            data-is-authenticated="{{ app.user ? '1' : '' }}"
            data-is-verified="{{ app.user and app.user.verified ? '1' : '' }}"
            data-csrf-token="{{ csrf_token('convert_google_maps') }}"
            data-credit-balance="{{ creditBalance }}"
            data-locale="{{ app.request.locale }}"
            data-capabilities="{{ capabilities|json_encode }}"
            data-landing-page="{{ landingPage }}"
            class="mt-3"
        ></div>
    </div>

    {{ vite_entry_script_tags('convertHero', { dependency: 'react' }) }}

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-16">
        {% include 'guides/_route_workflow.html.twig' with {
            steps: [
                { icon: 'map-pin', label: 'Google Maps' },
                { icon: 'sparkles', label: 'SmartGPX' },
                { icon: 'file-code', label: 'GPX' },
                { icon: 'navigation', label: 'OsmAnd' },
            ]
        } %}

        {% include 'guides/_how_to_steps.html.twig' with { i18n_prefix: 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand' } %}

        <div class="prose prose-sm mt-10 max-w-none">
            <h2>{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.osmand_specifics_title'|trans }}</h2>
            {% if 'fr' == app.request.locale %}
                <p>OsmAnd est l'application qui navigue elle-même, ce n'est pas un appareil séparé à
                synchroniser : l'import est donc plus simple. Ouvrez le fichier GPX téléchargé et
                choisissez « Ouvrir dans OsmAnd » depuis le menu de partage de votre téléphone, ou
                ouvrez OsmAnd et allez dans « Mes Endroits » → « Traces » pour l'importer
                manuellement. La trace atterrit dans votre dossier d'import. Vous pouvez ensuite lancer
                la navigation directement depuis la trace, et si le GPX contient plusieurs segments,
                OsmAnd vous laisse choisir lequel suivre.</p>

                <h2>{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.limitations_title'|trans }}</h2>
                <p>OsmAnd navigue avec son propre moteur de calcul d'itinéraire et le profil de
                navigation choisi (marche, vélo, voiture…) : la fidélité avec laquelle il suit le
                tracé importé dépend donc aussi de ce réglage, plutôt que de toujours reproduire le GPX
                point par point.</p>
            {% else %}
                <p>OsmAnd is the app doing the navigating, not a separate device to sync, so importing
                is simpler. Open the downloaded GPX file and choose "Open in OsmAnd" from your phone's
                share menu, or open OsmAnd itself and go to My Places, then Tracks, to import it
                manually. The track lands in your Import folder. From there you can start navigation
                directly from the track, and if the GPX has multiple segments, OsmAnd lets you pick
                which one to follow.</p>

                <h2>{{ 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.limitations_title'|trans }}</h2>
                <p>OsmAnd navigates using its own routing engine and whichever navigation profile
                you've selected (walking, cycling, driving, and so on), so how closely it follows the
                exact imported line can vary with that setting rather than always tracing the GPX
                point-for-point.</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {% include 'tools/_cta.html.twig' with { variant: 'chrome_extension' } %}

        {% include 'guides/_related.html.twig' with {
            links: [
                { route: 'app_guides_google_maps_to_gpx', icon: 'map-pin', label: 'guides.google_maps_to_gpx.title'|trans },
                { route: 'app_gpx_viewer', icon: 'sparkles', label: 'home.free_tools.gpx_viewer'|trans },
                { route: 'app_guides_google_maps_to_garmin', icon: 'route', label: 'guides.google_maps_to_garmin.title'|trans },
                { route: 'app_guides_google_maps_to_wahoo', icon: 'bike', label: 'guides.google_maps_to_wahoo.title'|trans },
            ]
        } %}

        {% include 'guides/_faq.html.twig' with {
            namespace: 'guides.google_maps_to_osmand.faq',
            keys: ['q_direct_export', 'q_convert', 'q_gpx_support', 'q_navigation', 'q_integration', 'q_multi_stop'],
        } %}

        <p class="mt-8 border-t border-border pt-6 text-xs text-muted-foreground">{{ 'guides.disclaimer'|trans }}</p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
